modify and redistribute their Covered Work for the Permitted Uses defined
below, for the duration of the applicable copyright. Except as provided in
Section 8, this grant cannot be withdrawn from a compliant recipient.

Permitted Uses are:

    a. Personal, hobby and other noncommercial experimentation.

    b. Noncommercial teaching, learning, demonstrations and scientific
       research, including work within schools, universities, research
       institutions and similar organizations. Institutional funding,
       grants, tuition and salaries do not, by themselves, make such work
       commercial. This permission does not include work directed at
       developing, testing, manufacturing or selling a commercial product
       or service, or research performed as a commercial service for a
       customer.

    c. Noncommercial modification and redistribution of the Covered Work
       for the purposes above, subject to Section 4.

Commercial Use requires separate written permission under Section 3.
Being a nonprofit organization, calling a project scientific or educational,
or making no profit on a particular transaction does not by itself exempt
a Commercial Use.

3. Commercial Use and Separate Permission

Commercial Use includes using, reproducing, modifying or distributing the
Covered Work:

    a. In a product offered for sale, lease or another commercial supply,
       including a controller, firmware package or other integrated product.

    b. To provide a paid service, including imaging, equipment operation,
       hosting, installation, technical support or standalone commercial
       training. Teaching permitted by Section 2.b remains permitted.

    c. In the development, testing, manufacture, marketing or delivery of
       a commercial product or service, including internal commercial R&D
       and use in the operation of a commercial activity.

A charge limited to the actual cost of copying or transmitting a permitted
redistribution of software or documentation, without profit or remuneration
for labor, does not alone make that redistribution commercial. This exception
does not authorize selling assembled hardware containing the Covered Work.

Voluntary donations or grants without a required payment, paid access,
paid feature or other commercial consideration do not alone make an
otherwise Permitted Use commercial.

Commercial permission must be granted in writing by the relevant rights
holder or their authorized representative. An agreement may define the
covered versions, recipient, products or services, duration, territory and
financial terms. Access to this repository, discussion of a project or
submission of a contribution is not commercial permission. For CanonXL
commercial licensing requests, open an issue at
https://github.com/NoxSilicium/CanonXL/issues/new.

